	abstract = {Traditional cybersecurity awareness programs often fail to instill lasting behavioral change due to their static, one-size-fits-all nature. This research addresses these shortcomings through the design, implementation, and evaluation of CyberSense AI, an intelligent mobile application that delivers adaptive, behavior-driven cybersecurity education. The system integrates three core innovations: (1) a personalized adaptive learning engine, (2) an interactive phishing simulation module for practical skill assessment, and (3) a live threat intelligence feed. The platform’s threat detection capability is powered by a custom-trained XGBoost machine learning model, which achieved an accuracy of 96% and a ROC AUC of 99% on a benchmark dataset, demonstrating high efficacy in identifying phishing threats. By synergizing real-time threat detection with personalized, interactive training, CyberSense AI provides a holistic framework that bridges the critical gap between theoretical knowledge and practical application, fostering a more resilient security culture. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.},
