	abstract = {Runtime verification systems require expressive yet executable specification languages to evaluate temporal system behavior with minimal overhead. This paper presents communicating finite state machines (CFSMs) as a direct and modular model for specifying and evaluating runtime properties inf multi-component environments. Unlike logic-based approaches that require synthesis, CFSMs enable structured, executable specifications that naturally capture message-driven semantics and process isolation. We present a complete CFSM framework implemented using a polling-based snapshot architecture, demonstrate its effectiveness in a hypervisor environment, and evaluate its ability to capture real-world performance degradations in virtualized network stacks. © 2025 IEEE.},
